@startuml raditrack_activity_examination_lifecycle
!theme plain
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 8
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam ActivityBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
skinparam ActivityBorderColor #334155

title RADiTrack — Activity Diagram: Examination Lifecycle & TAT Calculation

|Radiologic Technologist|
start
:Complete the imaging examination;
:Log the completed exam\n(accession no., modality, patient category);
note right
  Prototype: an Administrator logs it through
  Import exams or RIS Simulator → Log Completed Scan.
  Planned: from the RIS via the sync agent
  (after the hospital approves RIS access).
end note

|RADiTrack|
:Validate the exam\n(known modality & category, valid times);
if (Valid?) then (no)
  :Show the problem and\nreject the entry;
  stop
else (yes)
endif
:Save exam with status "Exam completed"\nand completion time **T1**;
:Record "Created" in the audit trail;
:Add exam to the reading backlog;
fork
  :Refresh dashboard KPIs\n(backlog count, scans);
fork again
  :Refresh Patient TV queue\n(no patient details);
end fork

|Radiologist|
:Open Examinations → Backlog\n(optionally filter by waiting time:\n< 1 day … 30 days or more);
if (Waiting time > SLA target?) then (yes)
  |RADiTrack|
  :Flag exam as\n"Past SLA, still unsigned";
  |Radiologist|
else (no)
endif
:Interpret images and\nsign off the report;

|RADiTrack|
if (Already signed off?) then (yes)
  :Refuse ("already signed off")\nand record the refused attempt;
  stop
else (no)
endif
:Record sign-off time **T2**;
:Calculate **TAT = T2 − T1**;
:Look up SLA target for the exam's\nmodality + patient category;
if (TAT > SLA target?) then (yes)
  :Mark report as\n**SLA breached** (signed late);
else (no)
  :Mark report as\n**within SLA** (met target);
endif
:Set status "Completed / signed off",\nremove from backlog and record\n"Signed off" in the audit trail;
fork
  :Update dashboard KPIs, charts\nand 7-day / 12-month views;
fork again
  :Update Patient TV queue;
fork again
  :Notify other open RADiTrack tabs;
end fork

note right
  From here the exam is **locked**: editing, cancelling,
  deleting or signing off again is refused. It changes only
  through an import within the amendment window that the
  administrator confirms; TAT stays on the first sign-off.
end note
stop

@enduml
